<Blueprint bind:t />

<Figures layout="steps">
	<OriginStep bind:t step="name">It begins with a name, and the + of its C++, the language llama.cpp is written in.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="plus">A plus with the icon’s own arms: 240 wide upright, {lower} deep across.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="l">Keep the top and right arms and leave the centre empty: an L inside the +, its stem and foot touching at one point.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="lean">In a flash the bolt leans it: the L slants 30° on the baseline, every edge at {deg}°, on a grid of ideal triangles, with the bolt inside.</OriginStep>
	<OriginStep bind:t step="soften">Round only the two outer corners. That is the Llama icon.</OriginStep>
</Figures>

<Sketch />

<Figures layout="rules">
	<Rule rule="blades">A tall blade and a short foot, offset to the right, touching at one point.</Rule>
	<Rule rule="angle">All four slanted edges lean at {deg}°: the blades are parallel parallelograms.</Rule>
	<Rule rule="diagonal">The upper blade’s right edge and the foot’s left edge are the same line, through the joint.</Rule>
	<Rule rule="split">{SPLIT} above, {lower} below: close to two thirds to one third.</Rule>
	<Rule rule="steps">Five steps of 120 span the {SIZE}: the feet, the joint and the foot’s corner all land on them.</Rule>
	<Rule rule="corners">Only the two 120° outer corners round off: cut back {trim}, on a circle of radius ≈ {r}.</Rule>
</Figures>

<Specs />
